ssvnc (enhanced tightvnc viewer with ssl/ssh support)

This is a VNC viewer which supports VNC sessions tunnelled over
encrypted connections. It also supports scaling the display [*].

Optional dependency: zulu-openjdk8 (or actually any of the JDKs
that support Java 1.4). ssvnc only uses Java for "ultraftp", which
is used only for the file transfer extension of the Windows-only
UltraVNC server. If you want to build this, install a suitable JDK
and run the script with ULTRAFTP=yes in the environment. Note that the
SlackBuild author has never tested ultraftp (due to lack of access to
any UltraVNC server); if it doesn't work for you, please fix it and
email me a patch.

[*] So far as the SlackBuild author knows, this is the only Linux VNC
client which supports client-side scaling. In fact, this is the only
reason it's been submitted to SlackBuilds.org.
